<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gračanica Monastery</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1321</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gračanica Monastery is a Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> monastery near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pristina">Pristina</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, built by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-milutin">Stefan Milutin</a> around 1321. Its five-domed church is one of the finest works of late Byzantine-style architecture in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, and its interior is covered with frescoes, including portraits of the royal founders. It is part of the World Heritage Site Medieval Monuments in Kosovo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gracanica-monastery.jpg" alt="Gračanica Monastery" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sasa Micic · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gra%C4%8Danica_Monastery,_2013-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
